# Implement configurable line-art extraction

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical evidence is domain structure, not an operating raster or PDF
renderer; the finite design acceptance is explicitly bounded.

Convert images to transparent single-color paths with levels, threshold,
cleanup, detail, minimum feature, and preview controls suitable for hand color.

Current executable evidence now freezes the accepted live-compatible boundary:
one source image identity plus caller-owned levels, threshold, cleanup, detail,
minimum-feature, and preview controls can produce an ordered transparent-black
vector-path result linked back to that source. Result validation rejects drift
in any control or source identity from the exact request, with control drift
checked first. Successful comparison now seals the exact request/result pair so
later vector or live projection can require source linkage without repeating
identity logic. A 128-case oracle crosses every six-control drift subset with
matching or changed source identity and requires direct/sealed parity across
both mismatch classes plus the exact-match path.

The control values remain generic and have no inferred defaults.

Image decoding, control units/ranges/semantics, path extraction, vector
geometry,
acceptance diagnostics, preview rendering, and final rendering remain open.

## Finite transparent single-ink line-art extraction contract

**Inputs:** one immutable admitted raster asset identity, pixel dimensions,
color/alpha metadata and explicit request controls for levels, threshold,
cleanup, detail, minimum physical feature and preview. **Outputs:** an
ordered set of transparent-background black vector paths preserving the
original source link, a read-only preview proposal, or a refusal. There is
no automatic photograph-to-single-pen conversion without reviewed loss.

**Finite source/controls:** first release accepts one well-formed opaque PNG
or JPEG image with known physical placement and an admitted decoder, bounded
at 8 MiB input and 4096 x 4096 pixels. Level normalization and a threshold
operate on a declared grayscale luminance transform. Cleanup removes only
connected components smaller than a declared minimum feature in mm, after
pixel-to-page scaling. The line-art result contains no white filled regions,
color, gray wash, opaque background or hidden raster image inside the path.

**Worked two-detail example:** source `photo-1` is a 64 x 64 pixel black
outline of a four-sided leaf on white with two internal veins. Its physical
placement is 40 x 40 mm. `Low` uses two gray levels, threshold `0.5`,
cleanup of isolated components smaller than 0.6 mm and minimum feature
0.6 mm, returning a leaf outline plus major vein. `High` uses the same
threshold, cleanup 0.2 mm and minimum feature 0.2 mm, retaining both fine
veins where independently verified. Each result is transparent except
source-linked black strokes and has its own exact control/asset identity.
No real paths are claimed to have been extracted by this description.

**Admission rule:** fixed source and all six control values must match the
returned path evidence. A preview at 96 DPI only visualizes the candidate;
explicit user acceptance and output capability must precede replacing a
colored or photographic source with line art. Unsupported alpha handling,
missing physical scale or ambiguous line continuity produces a typed
non-acceptance, not an invented cleanup. Preserve original image bytes.

**Refusal example:** a blurred color photograph without separable edges,
a 5000-pixel side, transparent source with unknown blending, or returned
paths linked to another asset refuses the request. Full-color photographs
remain unsupported in a single-pen Live mode until a separate reviewed
conversion produces admitted black paths; silence is not consent.

**Assumptions and limits:** the repository already has six-control/source
linkage for transparent black vector-result intent. Raster decode, edge
estimation, cleanup, vector tracing, min-feature measurement, preview paint
and real user acceptance are missing. The leaf paths above are theoretical,
not rendered or tested line art.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for source/control/result identity; theoretical for
  vector extraction and loss review, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** bounded image input, two detail settings, transparent black
  path target, source preservation and unsuitable-input refusal.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** actual raster-to-vector conversion,
  image decoder, preview renderer or approved Live conversion.
